infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Evolve v1 in place vs fork a v2 package
  desc Add a field, you evolve; change what the data means, you fork
  compares
    - label Evolve v1 in place
      children
        - label Additive only — new field, new tag, new RPC
          desc Unknown fields skip, absent fields default — safe in both directions
        - label Producer and consumer deploy in any order
          desc The property independent service deployment quietly depends on
        - label Cheap — one set of types, no double-running
          desc Nothing to sunset; buf breaking sees a clean addition
    - label Fork to a v2 package
      children
        - label Meaning changes — cents to decimal, splits, remodel
          desc Patching fields one at a time leaves the team unsure what a message means
        - label Parallel types and services, served side by side
          desc checkout.v1 and checkout.v2 from one binary; consumers migrate at their own pace
        - label Expensive — run both for months
          desc v1 gets a deprecation window and a shutdown date
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
